{"id": "hospices-revoked-after-1-26-billion", "title": "Four Bay Area hospice and home-health agencies share owners with ones Medicare revoked", "seconds": 139.7, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "e28d2888edea8586", "words": 426, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Medicare can end a hospice’s right to bill it, and list it as revoked.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.61, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s5", "kicker": "Revoked Medicare Providers and Suppliers (July 2026)", "text": "Each revocation goes on a federal list with a date and a reason.", "mark": "a date and a reason"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.58, 0.77, 0.85, 1.3, 1.51, 1.64, 1.84, 2.15, 2.25, 2.51, 2.69, 2.92]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "story[1]"], "text": "Four Bay Area agencies share owners with ones on that list.", "t0": 3.73, "t1": 6.46, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Four Bay Area agencies", "sub": "still enrolled in October 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.45, 0.73, 1.24, 1.51, 1.76, 1.91, 2.09, 2.16, 2.33]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "story[1]"], "text": "What did Medicare pay them in 2024?", "t0": 6.58, "t1": 8.76, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Four Bay Area agencies", "sub": "still enrolled in October 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.21, 0.58, 0.8, 0.93, 1.01, 1.21]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount"], "text": "20.2 million dollars.", "t0": 8.76, "t1": 10.47, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$20.2 million", "label": "paid in 2024 to the four still enrolled", "sub": "$7.1 million of it to the two in San Francisco"}, "emph": ["20.2"], "wt": [0.04, 0.33, 0.7, 0.84, 1.19]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["status", "story[0]"], "text": "It’s a lead, not a finding. The revocations are Medicare’s; the owner links are this project’s join.", "t0": 10.99, "t1": 17.03, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "The owner links are this project’s join of federal owner numbers"}, "emph": ["a lead, not a finding"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.23, 0.79, 0.92, 1.0, 1.57, 2.07, 2.72, 2.87, 3.9, 4.0, 4.28, 4.6, 4.79, 5.0, 5.51]}, {"scene": "sf", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "story[1]"], "text": "First, Owen Healthcare’s San Francisco hospice:", "t0": 17.25, "t1": 19.84, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Owen Healthcare LLC", "kicker": "San Francisco", "sub": "hospice", "chip": "$4,345,102 in 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.52, 0.76, 1.23, 1.37, 1.8]}, {"scene": "sf", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "story[1]"], "text": "4,345,102 dollars in 2024.", "t0": 19.84, "t1": 22.44, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Owen Healthcare LLC", "kicker": "San Francisco", "sub": "hospice", "chip": "$4,345,102 in 2024"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.26, 0.53, 0.82, 0.91, 1.25, 1.56, 1.64, 1.9]}, {"scene": "sf", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "Two of its owners also held an interest in Los Robles Healthcare, revoked in December 2025.", "t0": 22.56, "t1": 27.71, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "Owen Healthcare LLC", "sub": "San Francisco hospice"}, {"art": "question", "name": "2 owner numbers", "sub": "both individuals"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Los Robles Healthcare LLC", "sub": "San Diego, revoked 18 December 2025"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.18, 0.34, 0.73, 0.97, 1.12, 1.25, 1.57, 1.68, 1.93, 2.31, 3.07, 3.5, 3.59, 3.98, 4.25]}, {"scene": "sf", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "story[1]", "established[10]"], "text": "Blossom Ridge Health’s home-health agency: 2,713,653 dollars.", "t0": 27.83, "t1": 31.37, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Blossom Ridge Health LLC", "kicker": "San Francisco", "sub": "home-health agency", "chip": "$2,713,653 in 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.56, 0.84, 1.26, 1.9, 2.1, 2.26, 2.56, 2.71, 3.05]}, {"scene": "sf", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "Four of its owners held an interest in a Sacramento agency, revoked in August 2025.", "t0": 31.49, "t1": 36.03, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "Blossom Ridge Health LLC", "sub": "San Francisco home health"}, {"art": "question", "name": "4 owner numbers", "sub": "all individuals"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Blossom Ridge Home Health Agency LLC", "sub": "Sacramento, revoked 22 August 2025"}]}, "emph": ["Four"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.24, 0.43, 0.69, 0.84, 0.96, 1.28, 1.36, 1.44, 1.93, 2.66, 3.15, 3.24, 3.55, 3.7]}, {"scene": "sf", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "story[1]"], "text": "The reason listed for both: abuse of billing privileges, pattern or practice.", "t0": 36.15, "t1": 40.16, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "abuse of billing privileges: pattern or practice", "kicker": "The reason listed for both"}, "emph": ["abuse of billing privileges"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.32, 0.64, 0.81, 1.46, 1.76, 1.84, 2.12, 2.84, 3.14, 3.33]}, {"scene": "sf", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "Medicare holds these same files, and left both enrolled.", "t0": 40.68, "t1": 43.45, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Both still enrolled", "sub": "October 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.42, 0.62, 0.84, 1.12, 1.67, 1.76, 1.97, 2.23]}, {"scene": "east", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "story[2]"], "text": "In Oakland, Owen Healthcare’s home-health agency has the same two owners:", "t0": 43.67, "t1": 47.37, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Owen Healthcare LLC", "kicker": "Oakland", "sub": "home-health agency", "chip": "$2,410,211 in 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.67, 0.92, 1.39, 1.88, 2.27, 2.45, 2.59, 2.8, 3.0]}, {"scene": "east", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "story[2]"], "text": "2,410,211 dollars.", "t0": 47.37, "t1": 49.21, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Owen Healthcare LLC", "kicker": "Oakland", "sub": "home-health agency", "chip": "$2,410,211 in 2024"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.33, 0.45, 0.81, 0.96, 1.31]}, {"scene": "east", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[9]", "notEstablished[6]"], "text": "Its own 2024 cost report counts 59,210 visits. What did each one cost?", "t0": 49.33, "t1": 55.3, "shot": "b10a", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "59,210", "label": "visits in its 2024 cost report", "sub": "certification number 557796"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.32, 0.53, 1.03, 1.34, 1.69, 2.14, 2.6, 3.03, 3.26, 3.56, 3.82, 4.49, 4.79, 4.92, 5.08, 5.31]}, {"scene": "east", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[9]", "innocent[7]"], "text": "3.33 dollars, against 236 for the middle California agency. It may be a keying error.", "t0": 55.3, "t1": 61.96, "shot": "b10b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["$3.33 a visit", "Crossroads Home Health & Hospice, 2024 cost report"], "b": ["$236 a visit", "the middle California agency"], "kicker": "Cost per Medicare visit"}, "emph": ["3.33"], "wt": [0.04, 0.38, 0.87, 1.78, 2.22, 2.35, 2.63, 2.8, 3.28, 3.42, 3.55, 3.77, 4.32, 5.14, 5.37, 5.56, 5.68, 5.78, 6.16]}, {"scene": "east", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "story[2]"], "text": "In Pleasanton, Sojourn Hospice got the most: 10,762,074 dollars.", "t0": 62.48, "t1": 66.98, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Sojourn Hospice & Palliative Care -East Bay, LLC.", "kicker": "Pleasanton", "sub": "hospice", "chip": "$10,762,074 in 2024"}, "emph": ["the most"], "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.87, 1.28, 1.68, 1.85, 1.96, 2.54, 2.81, 3.02, 3.32, 3.48, 3.88]}, {"scene": "east", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[1]"], "text": "Its shared owner is a company, Bristol Hospice Holdings.", "t0": 67.1, "t1": 70.17, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "Sojourn Hospice", "sub": "Pleasanton"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Bristol Hospice Holdings Inc", "sub": "a company’s owner number"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Optimal Home Health Care Inc.", "sub": "Bakersfield, revoked 9 February 2025"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.44, 0.73, 0.9, 0.97, 1.65, 2.05, 2.39]}, {"scene": "east", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[1]"], "text": "It also held an interest in Optimal Home Health Care.", "t0": 70.29, "t1": 72.57, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "Sojourn Hospice", "sub": "Pleasanton"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Bristol Hospice Holdings Inc", "sub": "a company’s owner number"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Optimal Home Health Care Inc.", "sub": "Bakersfield, revoked 9 February 2025"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.32, 0.55, 0.63, 0.97, 1.13, 1.52, 1.76, 1.98]}, {"scene": "east", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "story[2]"], "text": "Revoked in February 2025, for an affiliation that poses an undue risk.", "t0": 72.69, "t1": 77.01, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "an affiliation that poses an undue risk", "kicker": "Revoked February 9, 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.49, 0.93, 1.13, 1.94, 2.06, 2.16, 2.72, 2.84, 3.22, 3.39, 3.91]}, {"scene": "dev", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[0]"], "text": "One Bay Area hospice is on the list itself: Devotion Hospice Care, in Hayward.", "t0": 77.23, "t1": 81.45, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Devotion Hospice Care Inc", "kicker": "Hayward", "sub": "on the federal revoked list"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.37, 0.65, 1.07, 1.16, 1.27, 1.36, 1.57, 2.43, 2.9, 3.3, 3.65, 3.76]}, {"scene": "dev", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[0]"], "text": "Revoked in April 2025.", "t0": 81.57, "t1": 83.24, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$2,492,518", "label": "paid over fiscal 2018 to 2024", "sub": "$1,964,944 of it in 2024"}, "emph": ["Revoked"], "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.45, 0.71, 0.96]}, {"scene": "dev", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[0]"], "text": "Before that, Medicare paid it 2,492,518 dollars.", "t0": 83.76, "t1": 86.88, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$2,492,518", "label": "paid over fiscal 2018 to 2024", "sub": "$1,964,944 of it in 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.7, 1.03, 1.22, 1.31, 1.56, 1.72, 2.02, 2.18, 2.59]}, {"scene": "dev", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "The reason is an affiliation, not a finding about what it billed.", "t0": 87.4, "t1": 90.37, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "affiliation that poses an undue risk", "kicker": "The listed reason"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.41, 0.52, 0.62, 1.53, 1.67, 1.75, 2.13, 2.33, 2.48, 2.61]}, {"scene": "state", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "story[4]"], "text": "The federal list names 479 revoked hospices. How many are in California?", "t0": 90.59, "t1": 96.31, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The federal list", "sub": "July 2026", "chip": "479 revoked hospices"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.42, 0.8, 1.13, 1.38, 1.66, 2.34, 2.88, 3.81, 4.26, 4.51, 4.63, 4.73]}, {"scene": "state", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "402.", "t0": 96.31, "t1": 97.6, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "402", "label": "of the 479 are in California", "sub": "and 43 California home-health agencies"}, "emph": ["402"], "wt": [0.04, 0.4, 0.78]}, {"scene": "state", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[3]"], "text": "Medicare had paid them more than a billion dollars. 411.2 million in 2024 alone.", "t0": 98.12, "t1": 103.99, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$1,264.7 million", "label": "paid to 339 of them, fiscal 2018 to 2024", "sub": "$411.2 million in 2024 alone: 9.5% of the State’s hospice payments"}, "emph": ["more than a billion"], "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.51, 0.71, 0.89, 1.03, 1.17, 1.26, 1.72, 2.4, 2.7, 2.99, 3.39, 3.7, 3.86, 4.33, 4.5, 4.7, 5.27]}, {"scene": "state", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[3]"], "text": "148 of them still hold an active State licence.", "t0": 104.11, "t1": 106.9, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "148", "label": "revoked hospices still hold an active State licence", "sub": "16 October 2026 listing; paid $149.7 million in 2024"}, "emph": ["148"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.38, 0.86, 0.94, 1.1, 1.42, 1.62, 1.75, 2.02, 2.29]}, {"scene": "state", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "The State still lists Los Robles and Optimal as open, too.", "t0": 107.02, "t1": 110.02, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Los Robles Healthcare LLC", "still listed as open"], "b": ["Optimal Home Health Care Inc", "still listed as open"], "kicker": "Tied to the Bay Area four"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.35, 0.56, 0.85, 1.1, 1.5, 1.7, 2.12, 2.3, 2.63]}, {"scene": "state", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why", "notEstablished[5]"], "text": "A State licence is separate: a licensed hospice can still serve Medi-Cal and private patients.", "t0": 110.14, "t1": 114.84, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "A State licence", "sub": "a separate permission from Medicare enrolment"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.28, 0.61, 0.73, 1.47, 1.55, 2.02, 2.35, 2.52, 2.69, 3.01, 3.5, 3.74, 4.09]}, {"scene": "state", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[5]", "suspicious[4].what"], "text": "Medi-Cal’s November listing still enrols 20 of the 402. None is in the Bay Area.", "t0": 114.96, "t1": 120.04, "shot": "b22a", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "20", "label": "of the 402 revoked California hospices still enrolled in Medi-Cal", "sub": "16 November 2026; none in the Bay Area"}, "emph": ["20 of the 402"], "wt": [0.0, 0.44, 0.79, 1.17, 1.38, 1.72, 2.09, 2.29, 2.39, 2.63, 2.89, 3.74, 4.07, 4.25, 4.35, 4.45, 4.67]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[2]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "Nothing shows a payment after a revocation. The files stop at 2024.", "t0": 120.26, "t1": 124.31, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Any payment after a revocation", "That any care was not given", "Misconduct by any agency or owner"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.41, 0.48, 0.76, 1.01, 1.08, 1.83, 2.25, 2.63, 2.91, 3.09, 3.35]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "A revocation is not a finding against any person, and it can be appealed.", "t0": 124.43, "t1": 128.08, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "it is not a finding against any person, and it can be appealed and reversed"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.66, 0.78, 0.91, 1.0, 1.38, 1.65, 1.81, 2.5, 2.59, 2.75, 2.99, 3.12]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]", "established[8]"], "text": "What would settle it? The notices, any appeals, and Medicare’s 2025 payments.", "t0": 128.2, "t1": 133.38, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The revocation notices and any appeal decisions"}, {"who": "", "what": "Medicare’s payments by provider for 2025"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.28, 0.53, 0.79, 1.31, 2.02, 2.23, 2.94, 3.08, 3.61, 3.74, 4.01, 4.55]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "No authority has made a finding against any agency still enrolled.", "t0": 133.5, "t1": 136.51, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.63, 0.76, 0.93, 1.04, 1.36, 1.66, 1.92, 2.3, 2.51]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 136.63, "t1": 138.84, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.3, 0.41, 0.53, 1.24, 1.39, 1.53]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The list", "sf": "San Francisco", "east": "The East Bay", "dev": "On the list itself", "state": "Across California", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "dossier", "hook": "document"}